# Validation (before every commit or push)

Run in order; all must pass (mirrors `.github/workflows/ci.yml`):

```bash
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm run verify:benchmarks
npm run test:run
npm run build
```

Do not claim completion or push without a green run.

## Prohibited CI weakening

- No `continue-on-error` on required steps
- No skipping commands
- No broadening ESLint ignores beyond existing project config
- No weakening assertions, deleting active benchmarks, or converting failing tests to `it.todo` for green CI
- No importing production calculator code into `scripts/verify-benchmarks.mjs`

# Git discipline

- Work on a **dedicated branch**; never commit directly to `main`
- Keep commits bounded and why-focused
- Use **draft PRs** for active phase work
- Confirm working tree is clean before and after git operations
- Branch naming: `feat/`, `fix/`, `test/` prefixes per repo convention

Push and draft-PR creation are allowed by default (see `settlerate-phase-and-agent-workflow.mdc`). Merge, ready-for-review, and branch deletion require explicit authorization.
